                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.51/1182: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bowers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-01-22T18:00:00-04:00">January 22, 1940—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 7:12 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>21. Department’s telegram No. 8, January 8, 3 p.m. Pedregal informs Embassy
                    confidentially that after three conversations with President Aguirre he is
                    encouraged to feel that Fomento plans may proceed perhaps on an installment
                    basis until political situation here becomes better settled. He tentatively
                    plans to leave by plane about February 1 for Washington.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
